    "result_text": "All 60 tests pass. `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nMoved date-derived values onto a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starts 1 July, named by the calendar year it ends \u2014 Australian convention, e.g. `FY26` = 1 Jul 2025 \u2013 30 Jun 2026).\n\n**New helper** \u2014 `rest/function/common/FiscalYear.java`:\n- `endingYear(date)` \u2014 the fiscal year's ending calendar year (Jan\u2013Jun \u2192 same year; Jul\u2013Dec \u2192 next year).\n- `label(date)` \u2014 `FY<YY>` (null-safe, returns `null` when no date).\n- `elapsed(from, to)` \u2014 elapsed fiscal years = difference of ending years (count of 1 July boundaries crossed).\n\n**Changes:**\n- **`fiscalYear` response field** \u2014 added `fiscalYear` (`FY<YY>`) to the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml`, wired in `OwnerMapper` via `FiscalYear.label(owner.getRegistrationDate())`. Since the registration date stored on the owner is already business-day-adjusted (`BuildOwner`), the fiscal year derives from the adjusted date.\n- **Membership identifier** \u2014 `AssignMembershipNumber` now builds the `-M<YY>` segment from the fiscal year (`FiscalYear.endingYear(...) % 100`) instead of the calendar year, so it always matches `fiscalYear`.\n- **Tenure** \u2014 `MembershipLevels` now awards the +3 tenure points for more than one *elapsed fiscal year* (`FiscalYear.elapsed(...) > 1`) rather than a 365-day window. A new owner still has zero tenure, so the level-3 cap for new owners is preserved.\n- Updated the `membershipNumber` and `membershipPoints` descriptions in `openapi.yml` to match.\n\nOn today's date (2026-08-21) new owners get `fiscalYear=FY27` and `membershipNumber=...-M27`, consistent across the two fields.\n\nOne judgment call worth flagging: no test exercises the tenure-points threshold with a real (backdated) tenure, so I translated the original \"more than 365 days\" (\u2248 more than one year) to \"more than one elapsed fiscal year\" (`elapsed > 1`). If you intended \"one or more elapsed fiscal years\" (`>= 1`), that's a one-line change in `MembershipLevels`.",
